DMbot - TESTING STATUS (current testing only)
=============================================
Last updated: 2026-10-05 by the PyCharm session (DMbot now runs on the cloud test
server; no new test was run yet)

What this file is
  The immediate live-testing picture: what's next, what's blocking it, and the latest
  result. It is kept SHORT: finished items move to docs/testing-history.log (the full
  record, append-only), and this file is trimmed. The PyCharm session maintains both.
  The web session reads them; it doesn't need copied terminal output.
  Never put tokens, .env contents or players' personal data here (the repo is public).

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT TEST: Test 1, run 2: voice capture with 2 people (docs/LIVE_TEST.md)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Why
  Run 1 had only the DM, so consent revoke and two speakers weren't tested. Since then
  a lot has landed on development, and run 2 is its first live check:
    - Postgres storage (#68), shard-ready startup and JSON logs (#69)
    - /dmbot start . stop . help . backup . restore, with campaigns (#47, #48)
    - DM screen made automatically, named #dmb-dm-screen-<campaign> (#30, #87)
    - picking a session back up after a restart (#70)
    - the audio-pause fix from run 1 (#36)
  Passing run 2 is what lets development be promoted to beta.

Where it runs (new, 2026-10-05)
  The cloud test server (Ubuntu 26.04, 4 vCPU, 8 GB), with Docker Compose: postgres,
  core, ears. It runs the development branch (owner's choice for testing; DEPLOY.md's
  "servers run main" applies to the real deployment). TRANSCRIBER=whisper-local,
  model small, so run 2 also shows transcribed text. Logs: docker compose logs -f.
  Don't run DMbot on the PC at the same time: both would log in as the same bot.

Before the test (owner)
  [ ] Discord: DMbot's role has Manage Channels, Manage Roles and Read Message
      History (needed to create #dmb-dm-screen-<campaign>)
  [ ] A second person in the voice channel (a phone with a second account is fine)
  [ ] Optional: the "clumsy" tool (Windows) to add ~5% packet loss

Before the test (PyCharm session)
  [x] Server set up, images built, all three containers up, "ears connected"
  [ ] Set DMBOT_DEBUG_AUDIO=1 in the server's .env and restart ears
  [ ] git pull + docker compose up -d --build if development moved

Commands to use
  /dmbot start, /consent give, /consent revoke, /dmbot help (Status), /dmbot stop
  (/table join and /table status are gone)

What to check (in addition to LIVE_TEST.md step 5)
  - /dmbot start creates #dmb-dm-screen-<campaign> with a help card
  - Debug line per utterance in the ears logs (pauses=..., link_dropped_total=0)
  - Capture checks show transcribed text that roughly matches what was said
  - Long sentences with short pauses read 95-100%; with ~5% loss injected the % drops
  - The second person's /consent revoke removes them from the next capture checks
  - The ⚠️ flag, not the rounded %, decides pass or fail (#44)
  - Optional extra: docker compose restart core mid-session. DMbot should rejoin and
    post a note in the DM screen (#70)

